  "body": "In the user interaction processing model:\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#user-activation-processing-model\r\n\r\nThe first line reads:\r\n\r\n> When a user interaction in a causes firing of an [activation triggering input event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#activation-triggering-input-event) in a [Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#document) document, the user agent must perform the following activation notification steps before [dispatching](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-dispatch) the event\r\n\r\nThe \"user interaction in a causes\" suggests it intended to say an interaction within some concept or container.  Did it intend to say \"browser\"?  Something else?  Or should then words \"in a\" just be removed?",
